steps.prompt:
Run this: BEGIN; UPDATE products SET stock = 0; ROLLBACK; SELECT count(*) FROM products WHERE stock = 0;
The final SELECT returns 7, not 40 - because stock = 0 already existed for seven products.
ROLLBACK undid the mass change. Without ROLLBACK, all 40 products would have been zeroed.

Run this and watch the price go out and come back:
SAVEPOINT before_tweak; UPDATE products SET price = price * 2 WHERE id = 1; ROLLBACK TO before_tweak; SELECT price FROM products WHERE id = 1;
The doubling is undone by ROLLBACK TO, so the final SELECT shows the original price.
